 going to start to  see a lot more tragic and difficult  cases carrie franklin director of ucla's  center on reproductive health law and  policy said since the nationwide right  to abortion was eliminated by the  supreme court these types of cases will  happen more often in a lot of  anti-abortion states people will find  themselves unable to terminate  pregnancies that are the product of rape  and incest and they will find themselves  in difficult traumatic situations  detective hewn said dna tests are being  conducted to confirm the paternity  fuentes is scheduled to be in court  again next week there has been no  comment from his defense attorney  it's a tough story the columbus dispatch  in ohio which has been covering the  stories you know elaine says that since  may 9 they found this is quoting them up  to 50 incidences police reports filed of  people young women under the age of 15  that have been raped this story really  illustrates just how complex this issue  is how deeply personal this issue is and  you know this is a case that has a lot  of americans reflecting and we're going  to hear i'm sure more about it and 10  years old it's just like ugh it's a  punch of the gut it's an awful lot  horrific it's an extreme case but it  shows the the extremity of the law in  about 11 states no exceptions elaine  thank you very much
 

